From bdf07a15f7b25bffcd0bca7b82069149691378dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:39:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/85] input: do not wait out the idle interval for the tail
 to finish

At the end of a pass the main loop waits for the decoders to report empty
before repeating, and it waited at the idle rate - a tenth of a second -
so the output had played dry and sat silent for up to that long before the
next pass was even asked for. Poll at a twentieth of that.

The wait itself stays: it is what holds playback to real time, the drain
not finishing until the audio has been heard. Only the slack goes, taking
the gap at each repeat from 50-125 ms to 25 ms, which is the resolution of
the measurement rather than an exact figure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input/input.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/input/input.c b/src/input/input.c
index bfc2e2f7bc..a95c2c2984 100644
--- a/src/input/input.c
+++ b/src/input/input.c
@@ -766,8 +766,11 @@ static void MainLoop( input_thread_t *p_input, bool b_interactive )
             }
             else if( !es_out_GetEmpty( input_priv(p_input)->p_es_out ) )
             {
+                /* Not at the idle rate: what follows a repeat cannot be asked
+                 * for until this reports empty, so a tenth of a second of
+                 * slack here is a tenth of a second of silence at every loop. */
                 msg_Dbg( p_input, "waiting decoder fifos to empty" );
-                i_wakeup = mdate() + INPUT_IDLE_SLEEP;
+                i_wakeup = mdate() + INPUT_IDLE_SLEEP / 20;
             }
             /* Pause after eof only if the input is pausable.
              * This way we won't trigger timeshifting for nothing */
